# Secrets — these must never enter a build context. `*.env` does not match a
# nested path (Docker's `*` does not cross `/`), which is how web-gateway/
# backend/.env — with a real Anvil SSH private key in it — ended up inside the
# backend image. Both forms, and the leading-dot form, are listed on purpose.
**/*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.local.example
**/secrets.yml
**/*_ed25519
**/*_ed25519.pub
**/*_rsa
**/*_rsa.pub

web-gateway/frontend/node_modules
web-gateway/frontend/.next
.git
.claude
.playwright-mcp
docs/
deploy/

# The private ops checkout — encrypted secrets and .sops.yaml. This repository
# has leaked a key through the build context once already (see the .env rule
# above); ops/ must never enter it.
ops/
